/**
@defgroup image_loading Image Loading

ImageLoader selects format-specific decoders and delivers decoded pixels and
progress to its callers. ImageLoaderBackend defines the decoder interface.
Start with image_loader_new(), image_loader_start(), and image_loader_get_pixbuf().

See @ref image_display_lifecycle for the complete selection-to-display flow.
See @ref ownership_loader for worker execution, signal delivery, cancellation,
and borrowed pixbuf lifetimes. Display and rendering APIs are in @ref rendering.
*/

/**
@defgroup rendering Rendering

ImageWindow manages displayed images, preloading, and presentation state.
PixbufRenderer handles zooming, orientation, source pixels, and tile callbacks;
RendererFuncs connects it to the tile backend.

See @ref image_display_lifecycle for how decoding and rendering overlap.
See @ref ownership_renderer for callback captures, pixbuf ownership, and snapshot
lifetimes. Decoding is covered by @ref image_loading, and reusable thumbnail data
by @ref caches.
*/

/**
@defgroup metadata Metadata

Read, format, edit, and write image metadata through @ref metadata.h and
@ref exif.h. The metadata layer coordinates pending writes, sidecars, keywords,
ratings, and color labels. The EXIF interface provides access to decoded tags
and embedded previews.

Use the metadata entry points for application-level edits rather than bypassing
the write queue. See @ref file_operations for operations that commit pending
metadata and @ref ownership_operations for their completion contracts.
*/

/**
@defgroup collections Collections

CollectionData owns an ordered collection of image entries. CollectInfo describes
an entry; @ref collect.h provides membership and ordering APIs, while
@ref collect-io.h handles loading, saving, and collection-manager updates.

Collection paths may differ from the directories containing their images.
Treat collection membership changes separately from filesystem operations in
@ref file_operations. Reference ownership is described in @ref ownership_basics.
*/

/**
@defgroup caches Caches

CacheData stores reusable image information, including dimensions, original
capture date, checksums, RGB similarity grids, and perceptual hashes. CacheLoader
loads or calculates requested cache fields. Thumbnail loaders and the in-memory
FileCache provide related reuse mechanisms; cache-maintenance APIs clean and
populate persistent caches.

Start with @ref cache.h, @ref cache-loader.h, and @ref thumb.h. Cache validity and
ownership remain the caller's responsibility where specified by each API.
See @ref image_loading for decoding and @ref metadata for metadata access.
*/

/**
@defgroup file_operations File Operations

@ref utilops.h provides user-facing copy, move, rename, delete, metadata-writing,
and editor operations. @ref ui-fileops.h provides synchronous filesystem helpers,
including file-tree traversal and transfer. file_tree_task_run() wraps threaded
folder operations with progress, cancellation, and main-context completion.

Read @ref ownership_operations before passing file lists or capturing window
state. The consuming list APIs, operation notifications, and threaded task
completion callbacks have different ownership and success semantics.
*/
